Manage the independent node inventory

Usage: xrm node [OPTIONS] [SUBCOMMAND]

OPTIONS:
  -h,   --help            Show this help message 

SUBCOMMANDS:
  add                     Save a manual node from typed settings, a share URI 
                          or native outbound JSON 
  list                    List saved nodes without connection secrets 
  show                    Show a node summary; --json includes editable 
                          connection settings 
  edit                    Edit one typed 
                          transport/security/sockopt/finalmask/mux subobject 
  replace                 Replace a manual node's name and typed/native 
                          settings 
  copy                    Copy a node as an independent manual node 
  remove                  Remove an unreferenced manual node 
  enable                  Enable a node 
  disable                 Disable a node 
  alias                   Set or clear a node display alias 
  labels                  Set node labels as comma-separated values 
  history                 Preview and confirm source-local redundant history 
                          cleanup 
  test                    Explicit ICMP, TCP, proxy URL or bounded download 
                          test 
  test-results            Show this Server session's observed node tests 
  test-cancel             Cancel one in-flight node test 

GLOBAL OPTIONS (before the command):
        --socket PATH     xrmd Unix domain socket 
        --json            Write machine readable output 
        --verbose         Include original diagnostics in human errors 

Examples:
  xrm node list
  xrm node add --name Direct --outbound-json '{"protocol":"freedom","settings":{}}'

Next: xrm node <command> --help
